---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    I am a human–computer interaction researcher exploring how AI-mediated, multi-modal interfaces can support everyday health, communication, and aging. My work sits at the intersection of conversational systems, lightweight visualisations, and mobile experiences, with an emphasis on accessibility, privacy, and respectful, boundary-aware design for aging populations and their families, caregivers. I’m interested in problems that scale—turning real-world signals into simple, helpful interactions, evaluating user trust and understanding, and translating insights into deployable products. I previously served as a research assistant with the Relational Agents Group at Northeastern University. I am now a PhD student in Computer Science at the University of Waterloo, supervised by Dr. Jim Wallace and Dr. Keiko Katsuragawa.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="University of Waterloo, Doctor of Philosophy in Computer Science (HCI)"
      subtitle="[2024.9] to [2028.8] (Expected) at [Waterloo], [Ontario], [Canada]"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Northeastern University, Master of Computer Science"
      subtitle="[2022.9] to [2024.8] at [Boston], [Massachusetts], [United States] // GPA: 3.94/4.00"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="University of Southern California, Master of Laws with Graduate Certificate in Technology and Entrepreneurship Laws"
      subtitle="[2021.8] to [2022.5] at [Los Angeles], [California], [United States] // Merit-based Scholarship $8000"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Durham University, Bachelor of Laws"
      subtitle="[2017.10] to [2020.8] at [College of St Hild and St Bede], [Durham], [United Kingdom]"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Part-time Product Manager"
      subtitle="Feb 2026 - Present at Early-Stage Soccer/Football Mobile Startup, Remote"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
        <li>Synthesize stakeholder input, prior documentation, and Figma prototypes into requirements for 10+ features to scope a V2 mobile product.</li>
        <li>Use heuristic and competitive research, user-flow analysis, annotated Figma specifications, and prioritization to identify design, privacy, implementation, and future usability-testing needs.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="UX Researcher & Engineer (Graduate Research Assistant)"
      subtitle="Sep 2024 - Present at HCI and Health Lab, University of Waterloo, Waterloo, Ontario, Canada"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
        <li>Lead end-to-end mixed-methods research on how families evaluate AI-mediated updates: recruit and manage participants, design Qualtrics surveys, run a 10-day mobile diary/ESM study and conduct semi-structured interviews; translate findings into product recommendations.</li>
        <li>Designed and ran a 4-week in-home field study of a tablet communication app, combining onboarding, longitudinal support, surveys, interviews, and usage logs to identify usability, privacy, and communication needs.</li>
        <li>Independently built and deployed a family-engagement Android app in Java/Firebase, from product design and UI/UX through implementation and user testing; translated co-design and field evidence into interaction flows, prototypes, requirements, and iteration priorities.</li>
        <li>Collaborated on an Expert-By-Experience (EBE) study and co-design workshop to gather insights and refine concepts for technologies that facilitate aging in place.</li>
        <li>Developed usage scenarios and personas to propose and evaluate ideas, ensuring practical and user-centered design solutions.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="Instructional Apprentice / Graduate Teaching Assistant"
      subtitle="Sep 2024 - Present at University of Waterloo, Waterloo, Ontario, Canada"
    >
      <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
        <li>CS 348 Introduction to Database Systems (from May 2025): Guide teams of 4-5 students through semester-long database-driven application projects covering SQL, schema design, user flows, implementation, testing, and milestone delivery. Advise on full-stack development with React frontends and Node.js or FastAPI backends.</li>
        <li>Coordinate assignment, project, and exam marking across the CS 348 TA team to support consistent, on-time assessment.</li>
        <li>CS 431/631 Data-Intensive Distributed Computing (Jan - Apr 2025): Provided individualized grading decisions for more than 20 variants of student answers involving TF-IDF, n-grams, and inverted index design, consistently evaluating technical correctness and conceptual clarity.</li>
        <li>Assessed understanding of search engine optimization techniques, including posting list sorting and binary search based on document ID ordering, and trade-offs in inverted index sorting for efficient retrieval, distributed processing, and MapReduce-style architectures.</li>
        <li>CS 115 Introduction to Computer Science 1 (Sep - Dec 2024): Graded assignments, midterms, and exams for over 100 students learning functional programming in Dr. Racket. Developed a detailed grading workflow aligned with course rubrics and provided constructive feedback to support student performance and consistent assessment.</li>
      </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
      title="HCI Researcher (Graduate Research Assistant)"
      subtitle="Apr 2023 - Jun 2024 at Relational Agents Group, Northeastern University, Boston, Massachusetts, USA"
    >
      <ul  class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
    <li>Conducted comprehensive data analysis for the SCC smartphone app, identifying user behavior trends and insights from a dataset involving over 500 participants, contributing to public health initiatives promoting vaccination and healthy lifestyles.</li>
    <li>Designed and conducted a user study to assess embodied conversational agents for pain assessment, collected and analyzed responses, and translated results and iterative feedback into design recommendations, contributing to a peer-reviewed ICMI publication.</li>
    <li>Performed empirical studies with strict adherence to research protocols, enabling the collection of high-quality, user-centric data to inform the development of health-focused conversational agents.</li>
    <li>Collaborated with interdisciplinary teams to prototype and refine interactive technologies, enhancing user engagement and addressing usability challenges in healthcare and wellness applications.</li>
    <li>Tested and troubleshot user interfaces and applications, systematically identifying usability issues and implementing solutions to optimize user experience.</li>
    <li>Maintained meticulous records and documentation of research findings, contributing to data-driven decision-making for HCI-focused projects.</li>
    </ul>
    </TimeLineElement>

    <TimeLineElement
